devex: Go example suggestion using a goroutine + channel so callers can cancel early:
```go
ctx, cancel := context.WithTimeout(context.Background(), 20*time.Second)
ch := make(chan string)

go func() { // streamer
  defer close(ch)
  for attempt := 0; attempt < 4; attempt++ {
    stream, err := client.Stream(ctx, &pb.Req{Prompt: prompt})
    if err != nil { time.Sleep(time.Duration(1<<attempt) * 100 * time.Millisecond); continue }
    for {
      tok, err := stream.Recv()
      if err == io.EOF { return }
      if err != nil { return }
      select {
      case ch <- tok.Content:
      case <-ctx.Done():
        return
      }
    }
  }
}()

// consumer side can cancel early
for s := range ch { fmt.Print(s) }
cancel()
```
clare: Nice pattern. I'll fold that into the Go snippet section and note that callers should respect context cancellation to avoid leaked goroutines.
